Benchmark patch for AWS-LC (https://github.com/aws/aws-lc) at commit
a3d1e685552f05a9ad04a2946962c03e97bdecac. Not part of AWS-LC.

It adds fifteen lines to crypto/fipsmodule/ml_dsa/mldsa/sign.c: for each
ML-DSA parameter set, a conditional include of the two prepared-key adapter
files in adapters/. Nothing in that file is removed or changed, and no other
file of AWS-LC is touched. The SHA-256 of the file before the patch is
b4fddbdd7c0e6acb50683dc96319ef9a77c34d7fc6ea24c7ec40bf1a567afe66, and after it
bc6d308d5416932c1f886c3dbfe3763b1eb4b9c618345795b2a7a1adbcb03d48.

The context lines of this patch are text of that file:
  Copyright (c) The mldsa-native project authors
  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT
as distributed in AWS-LC:
  Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. All Rights Reserved.
  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 OR ISC

Changes: the added lines only. The included adapter files and the prepared-key
entry points they define belong to this repository, not to AWS-LC.

Copyright (c) 2026 a16z
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

Apply from the root of an AWS-LC checkout at that commit:
  git apply /path/to/aws-lc-prepared-adapters.patch

